<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algirdas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1296–1377</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Olgierd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Algirdas was grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1345 to 1377. Through his marriage to the heiress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vitebsk">Vitebsk</a> he ruled that principality from about 1320, and as grand duke he expanded Lithuanian rule over much of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> at Blue Waters in 1362 and besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algirdas.jpg" alt="Algirdas" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: en:Alexander Guagnini (1538-1614) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Algirdas_kunigaik%C5%A1tis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
